1
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:46,440
{\an8}Surprised I'm still alive, sir?

2
00:01:46,520 --> 00:01:48,120
{\an8}I'm like a cornered dog.

3
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:51,160
{\an8}<i>But a cornered dog</i>
<i>is willing to risk everything.</i>

4
00:01:51,240 --> 00:01:54,480
{\an8}That only works
when both sides are of equal value.

5
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:56,720
{\an8}You think your life is worth that much?

6
00:01:56,800 --> 00:02:01,920
{\an8}You'll have about five hours
to break through the security system,

7
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,960
{\an8}<i>then find the safe and get the money out.</i>

8
00:02:05,040 --> 00:02:06,560
{\an8}Look at this.

9
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:09,720
{\an8}-Wow!
-Yes!

10
00:02:10,480 --> 00:02:14,000
{\an8}<i>Weren't you supposed to call the police</i>
<i>after we moved all the money out?</i>

11
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:17,200
{\an8}-<i>Exactly.</i>
-<i>Everyone, we've been set up.</i>

12
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:18,320
{\an8}<i>We need to get out of here now.</i>

13
00:02:18,999 --> 00:02:19,839
{\an8}Take cover!

14
00:02:19,920 --> 00:02:21,839
-Go! Move!
-Go!

15
00:02:21,920 --> 00:02:23,040
-Hurry up! Risa.
-Move!

16
00:02:25,640 --> 00:02:26,880
Wait.

17
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:30,320
They're inside the house.

18
00:02:36,960 --> 00:02:38,920
Sergeant, stay here. Don't move.

19
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:43,760
-Koh!
-Get out first!

20
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:45,000
Where are you going?

21
00:02:45,080 --> 00:02:46,080
I'm going to draw them away.

22
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:49,800
-Go!
-Wait, Koh!

23
00:02:49,880 --> 00:02:52,320
Hurry up. The cops are here. Hide.

24
00:02:56,720 --> 00:02:58,720
He's heading that way. After him!

25
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:17,680
This way.

26
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:19,440
Hurry.

27
00:03:33,040 --> 00:03:34,720
Which room did he hide in?

28
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:36,480
Check every room.

29
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:38,640
You check that room. I'll take this one.

30
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:44,920
Go.

31
00:03:59,440 --> 00:04:01,800
Go. Hurry up.

32
00:04:03,640 --> 00:04:04,560
This way.

33
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:06,520
Hong, come on.

34
00:04:08,640 --> 00:04:09,840
Hurry, this way.

35
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:17,200
Stop! Hey, stop!

36
00:04:24,640 --> 00:04:25,800
They're out back!

37
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:28,040
After them.

38
00:04:37,320 --> 00:04:39,280
Where's Yak? Where is he?

39
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:41,400
Yak!

40
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:44,560
Gao! Hurry, this way!

41
00:04:52,520 --> 00:04:53,440
This way, Hong.

42
00:04:55,080 --> 00:04:56,160
Go.

43
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:02,200
Girl, hurry.

44
00:05:02,280 --> 00:05:03,600
Just a second.

45
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:06,800
Stop!

46
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:19,920
Stop!

47
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:22,280
Risa!

48
00:05:26,760 --> 00:05:28,040
Risa!

49
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:29,480
I got this.

50
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:48,680
Yak, what do we do?

51
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:50,560
Go first.

52
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:52,880
Drive! Hurry!

53
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,360
Move it! Go!

54
00:05:55,440 --> 00:05:57,240
-Go now!
-Risa!

55
00:06:04,320 --> 00:06:05,440
Sergeant, after them!

56
00:06:05,520 --> 00:06:06,800
Yes, sir.

57
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:52,000
I need backup now. Hurry.

58
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:21,760
Mungkorn?

59
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:29,120
Mungkorn!

60
00:07:31,760 --> 00:07:33,040
Mungkorn!

61
00:07:46,760 --> 00:07:48,640
Mungkorn!

62
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:06,480
CHUCHI FESTIVAL 12 YEARS AGO

63
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:07,920
Mungkorn.

64
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:12,120
Mungkorn, come down.

65
00:08:28,080 --> 00:08:28,960
What are you doing?

66
00:08:30,960 --> 00:08:33,240
We're burning money for your grandparents
to use in the afterlife.

67
00:08:35,880 --> 00:08:36,960
Burning money?

68
00:08:38,280 --> 00:08:41,960
It's not real money.
It's called Gong Tek, joss paper.

69
00:08:46,800 --> 00:08:51,200
"Gong" means action,
and "Tek" means virtue.

70
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:54,240
Every Chinese New Year,
we burn these offerings

71
00:08:54,320 --> 00:08:57,600
to dedicate merit to our ancestors
who have passed away.

72
00:08:58,240 --> 00:09:01,240
It's a way of showing
our gratitude, you know?

73
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:06,440
One day, when your mom and I are gone,
you'll have to burn these for us too.

74
00:09:06,520 --> 00:09:08,520
Yes, Dad.

75
00:09:13,440 --> 00:09:15,760
You should go inside.
The smoke's too thick.

76
00:09:15,840 --> 00:09:17,640
You'll keep coughing.

77
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:20,480
Dad.

78
00:09:21,120 --> 00:09:24,440
Besides today being Chinese New Year,
what else is it?

79
00:09:26,840 --> 00:09:28,000
What day?

80
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:30,760
It's Ancestors' Day.

81
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:35,640
Or…

82
00:09:36,160 --> 00:09:37,000
Wednesday?

83
00:09:39,800 --> 00:09:42,160
You really forgot, didn't you?

84
00:09:45,800 --> 00:09:46,760
I was just joking, son.

85
00:09:48,480 --> 00:09:49,440
Here.

86
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:53,120
How could I forget your birthday?

87
00:09:54,640 --> 00:09:55,800
Happy birthday.

88
00:09:57,760 --> 00:09:59,240
Thank you, Dad.

89
00:10:00,520 --> 00:10:01,560
Watch out.

90
00:10:10,560 --> 00:10:12,400
<i>THE GREED OF THE OLD FARMER</i>

91
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:14,000
A storybook.

92
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:15,680
-Do you like it?
-I do.

93
00:10:30,160 --> 00:10:31,360
Rad.

94
00:10:32,760 --> 00:10:33,840
Come on. Let me help you.

95
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:37,960
Sit down first.

96
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:55,440
Rad!

97
00:10:58,760 --> 00:11:02,040
Rad!

98
00:11:02,120 --> 00:11:04,720
What's wrong? Rad!

99
00:11:05,320 --> 00:11:07,440
Mungkorn, go get the car keys!

100
00:11:09,040 --> 00:11:10,480
Rad! Mungkorn!

101
00:11:11,320 --> 00:11:12,200
Hurry, go get them!

102
00:11:17,480 --> 00:11:20,520
<i>Ms. Jutharad has stage-three lung cancer.</i>

103
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:25,200
<i>The cancer has spread to the lymph nodes</i>
<i>on the other side of her chest,</i>

104
00:11:25,280 --> 00:11:27,040
<i>near the collarbone.</i>

105
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:31,920
<i>We also found</i>
<i>multiple tumors in her lungs.</i>

106
00:11:32,440 --> 00:11:35,320
She needs surgery immediately.

107
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:37,760
Surgery right away?

108
00:11:38,520 --> 00:11:39,360
Yes.

109
00:11:40,520 --> 00:11:43,200
This is the initial cost estimate
for the surgery.

110
00:11:44,360 --> 00:11:47,240
If the family agrees
to proceed with treatment,

111
00:11:47,320 --> 00:11:50,720
you only need to pay
the initial surgery deposit.

112
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:54,640
After that, the hospital
will bill you every three days.

113
00:11:56,280 --> 00:11:57,520
Boss.

114
00:11:58,040 --> 00:12:02,680
I wouldn't be calling you for money
if I wasn't desperate.

115
00:12:03,920 --> 00:12:06,720
My wife needs urgent surgery.

116
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:10,080
Please help me. I'll do any job you want.

117
00:12:10,680 --> 00:12:13,640
Boss, please help me. Damn it.

118
00:12:30,200 --> 00:12:34,680
Mom, if you're sick,
why aren't you staying in the hospital?

119
00:12:36,920 --> 00:12:38,840
Why did you bring her home, Dad?

120
00:12:42,920 --> 00:12:47,000
I'm not that sick.
The doctor said I could go home.

121
00:12:47,680 --> 00:12:48,640
Really?

122
00:12:49,680 --> 00:12:50,760
Yes.

123
00:12:52,120 --> 00:12:54,960
You know what?

124
00:12:55,040 --> 00:12:57,840
The doctor said the best medicine for me

125
00:12:58,680 --> 00:12:59,760
is happiness.

126
00:13:01,440 --> 00:13:04,800
That's why I wanted to come home,

127
00:13:05,560 --> 00:13:08,240
to be with you and Dad.

128
00:13:08,840 --> 00:13:13,240
Because this house is where I'm happiest.

129
00:13:16,680 --> 00:13:18,360
Let's go inside.

130
00:14:08,400 --> 00:14:11,560
How are you so sure
that Dragon Boy took Risa?

131
00:14:11,640 --> 00:14:14,800
How many times do I have to tell you?
I saw it with my own eyes.

132
00:14:15,640 --> 00:14:18,040
I told you. Mungkorn's
been acting really strange.

133
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:21,520
Yeah. He disappeared during the mission.

134
00:14:21,600 --> 00:14:24,200
Then, after Admin's plan fell apart,
he suddenly showed up again

135
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:25,960
and took Risa with him.

136
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:27,840
Why are you all saying that?

137
00:14:28,920 --> 00:14:32,320
He might've just come to help Ris escape.

138
00:14:32,400 --> 00:14:34,160
He'd never hurt her.

139
00:14:35,240 --> 00:14:37,400
I kind of agree with Angpao.

140
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:40,920
There's no reason Mungkorn
would do something like that.

141
00:14:41,520 --> 00:14:42,600
Hey, Angpao.

142
00:14:43,440 --> 00:14:44,320
Check this laptop for me.

143
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:47,680
Is this really the time for this, Koh?

144
00:14:47,760 --> 00:14:48,960
Just do it.

145
00:14:51,280 --> 00:14:52,680
Wait.

146
00:14:52,760 --> 00:14:54,040
Mungkorn's laptop?

147
00:14:55,360 --> 00:14:56,760
How did you get this?

148
00:15:00,080 --> 00:15:01,280
Are you sure

149
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:03,320
this is Mungkorn's laptop?

150
00:15:03,400 --> 00:15:06,240
Yeah, of course I know.
It's my friend's laptop.

151
00:15:08,960 --> 00:15:10,800
What? What is it?

152
00:15:11,920 --> 00:15:15,560
I found it on the second floor
of Wisut's house.

153
00:15:35,600 --> 00:15:36,680
<i>Hello, everyone.</i>

154
00:15:37,400 --> 00:15:40,280
<i>Congratulations on the last mission.</i>

155
00:15:40,360 --> 00:15:42,120
<i>Everything went smoothly.</i>

156
00:16:38,720 --> 00:16:41,840
<i>I was in a hurry,</i>
<i>so I only managed to grab the laptop.</i>

157
00:16:44,440 --> 00:16:45,520
And…

158
00:16:46,520 --> 00:16:47,880
another hoodie.

159
00:16:49,040 --> 00:16:50,880
What are you talking about, Koh?

160
00:17:12,720 --> 00:17:13,800
Hold on.

161
00:17:29,600 --> 00:17:30,879
Mungkorn is Admin.

162
00:17:33,240 --> 00:17:36,240
This is ridiculous.

163
00:17:36,320 --> 00:17:37,960
Stop making baseless accusations.

164
00:17:38,560 --> 00:17:39,640
Then can you contact him?

165
00:17:39,720 --> 00:17:41,720
Well, no. But so what?

166
00:17:42,560 --> 00:17:44,680
Just wait until he comes back to base,
then ask him.

167
00:17:44,760 --> 00:17:46,040
Enough!

168
00:17:48,840 --> 00:17:50,800
Let's just turn it on

169
00:17:50,880 --> 00:17:52,840
and see what's inside.

170
00:17:52,920 --> 00:17:56,040
We'll find out
if he's been hiding anything from us.

171
00:17:58,560 --> 00:18:00,000
That's it.

172
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:01,840
Just turn it on.

173
00:18:24,880 --> 00:18:28,920
{\an8}AMBULANCE

174
00:18:37,680 --> 00:18:39,000
Boss.

175
00:18:39,080 --> 00:18:40,400
You look younger than ever.

176
00:18:40,480 --> 00:18:42,200
I used to be young. Now I'm old.

177
00:18:42,280 --> 00:18:43,800
You're not old at all, boss.

178
00:18:43,880 --> 00:18:47,400
-You can get injections now.
-Just do the whole face.

179
00:18:47,480 --> 00:18:49,120
-These days, you can do that.
-Sir.

180
00:18:49,200 --> 00:18:50,560
-Huh?
-It's urgent.

181
00:18:51,400 --> 00:18:52,880
Excuse me for a moment.

182
00:18:52,960 --> 00:18:55,360
Sure, boss. Probably
his girlfriend calling.

183
00:18:55,440 --> 00:18:57,880
Don't be ridiculous.

184
00:19:11,520 --> 00:19:12,400
Hello, sir.

185
00:19:17,760 --> 00:19:18,640
Are you okay, Captain?

186
00:19:20,880 --> 00:19:22,160
I'm fine.

187
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:26,080
I'm sorry we let the suspects escape.

188
00:19:29,480 --> 00:19:30,440
Forget it.

189
00:19:31,720 --> 00:19:34,680
Has the homeowner been notified
about the break-in?

190
00:19:35,280 --> 00:19:38,200
Yes, sir. Mr. Wisut is on his way back.

191
00:19:39,120 --> 00:19:40,280
Do we know how much was taken?

192
00:19:42,240 --> 00:19:43,640
We're still checking.

193
00:19:54,880 --> 00:19:56,160
-Hey.
-I'm in.

194
00:19:59,720 --> 00:20:01,440
NOVEL DRAFTS

195
00:20:01,520 --> 00:20:02,720
THE SCAM THAT CHANGED THE WORLD

196
00:20:02,800 --> 00:20:04,120
CHAPTER ONE

197
00:20:05,720 --> 00:20:07,720
See? There's nothing here.

198
00:20:07,800 --> 00:20:11,080
Just his university work and novel drafts.

199
00:20:11,160 --> 00:20:12,720
THE SCAM THAT CHANGED THE WORLD

200
00:20:14,800 --> 00:20:16,760
You guys don't study economics.

201
00:20:18,120 --> 00:20:19,400
Why is this folder here?

202
00:20:20,400 --> 00:20:21,760
-Yeah, you're right.
-Open it.

203
00:20:25,480 --> 00:20:28,320
BOSS KLUAY - HUMAN TRAFFICKING, M POWER
CALL CENTER, VS GROUP, HYENA888, ET 1ST

204
00:20:32,600 --> 00:20:33,720
BOSS KLUAY - HUMAN TRAFFICKING

205
00:20:33,800 --> 00:20:35,000
BOSS KLUAY - HUMAN TRAFFICKING

206
00:20:35,080 --> 00:20:36,040
SCREENSHOT

207
00:20:36,120 --> 00:20:37,360
BOXING CAMP BOSS ARRESTED
OVER HUMAN TRAFFICKING RING

208
00:20:47,560 --> 00:20:49,880
Why does Mungkorn have all this?

209
00:20:51,240 --> 00:20:52,240
He has everything.

210
00:20:53,680 --> 00:20:55,640
ET First?

211
00:22:16,640 --> 00:22:19,600
Sir, something's strange.
The criminals opened the safe,

212
00:22:19,680 --> 00:22:22,120
but they didn't take
any of the cash or valuables.

213
00:22:25,520 --> 00:22:26,880
How much cash was inside?

214
00:22:26,960 --> 00:22:28,920
Around 13 million baht.

215
00:22:36,960 --> 00:22:38,720
TEN HOURS EARLIER

216
00:22:38,800 --> 00:22:40,880
<i>Hello, General.</i>

217
00:22:43,120 --> 00:22:44,400
So you're Admin.

218
00:22:45,120 --> 00:22:48,000
I'm glad we finally get to speak.

219
00:22:48,840 --> 00:22:49,840
What do you want?

220
00:22:51,200 --> 00:22:55,080
<i>I have an offer for you.</i>

221
00:22:56,840 --> 00:23:00,560
Soon, there will be a robbery
at Wisut's house.

222
00:23:01,520 --> 00:23:05,480
You'll be in charge
of investigating the case.

223
00:23:07,440 --> 00:23:09,200
Why should I do what you say?

224
00:23:10,480 --> 00:23:13,360
There will be over 800 million baht

225
00:23:14,040 --> 00:23:17,360
<i>in illegal money inside that house.</i>

226
00:23:18,160 --> 00:23:22,320
But you must wait until my people

227
00:23:22,400 --> 00:23:24,080
finish setting everything up.

228
00:23:25,080 --> 00:23:26,240
You can't go in.

229
00:23:26,320 --> 00:23:27,600
Move.

230
00:23:28,200 --> 00:23:31,120
This is my house. Who are you to stop me?

231
00:23:37,040 --> 00:23:38,200
You're handling this case?

232
00:23:38,280 --> 00:23:39,480
Yes.

233
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:42,000
I, Police Lieutenant General
Thammarong Intharasa,

234
00:23:42,080 --> 00:23:46,000
am in charge of this investigation.
Please cooperate with the authorities.

235
00:23:50,280 --> 00:23:51,240
{\an8}FORENSIC EQUIPMENT

236
00:23:59,120 --> 00:24:01,400
What exactly did the criminals take?

237
00:24:01,480 --> 00:24:03,560
I should be asking you that.

238
00:24:03,640 --> 00:24:07,040
From what we've seen,
they didn't intend to steal anything.

239
00:24:07,120 --> 00:24:10,640
Otherwise, the 13 million baht in the safe

240
00:24:11,560 --> 00:24:12,880
would've been gone.

241
00:24:17,240 --> 00:24:20,680
If nothing's missing,
then why are you still here?

242
00:24:20,760 --> 00:24:24,120
You can all leave now. I want to rest.

243
00:24:24,640 --> 00:24:26,200
That's not possible.

244
00:24:26,800 --> 00:24:30,680
The break-in already happened.
We have to follow proper procedure.

245
00:24:31,480 --> 00:24:33,440
Please cooperate with the investigation.

246
00:24:44,640 --> 00:24:47,520
{\an8}Hey, you don't need to go that far.

247
00:24:48,480 --> 00:24:50,840
I'll file a report
for any missing items later.

248
00:24:51,760 --> 00:24:54,160
You're just making things
more complicated than they need to be.

249
00:24:54,240 --> 00:24:57,600
You should be out
catching real criminals instead.

250
00:25:04,760 --> 00:25:05,640
I understand.

251
00:25:07,800 --> 00:25:09,720
Good. Then please leave.

252
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:13,840
You can go now.

253
00:25:30,960 --> 00:25:32,480
What do you think you're doing?

254
00:26:14,800 --> 00:26:17,400
I'll need you to open
this safe for inspection.

255
00:26:18,280 --> 00:26:20,920
I trust all your assets

256
00:26:21,960 --> 00:26:23,560
are still accounted for.

257
00:26:43,160 --> 00:26:45,680
ANGPAO

258
00:26:56,560 --> 00:26:57,480
So?

259
00:26:58,440 --> 00:26:59,320
He's not answering.

260
00:27:05,680 --> 00:27:08,880
If Mungkorn is Admin, and you found
this laptop at Wisut's house,

261
00:27:08,960 --> 00:27:12,240
what's the connection between them?

262
00:27:12,840 --> 00:27:14,040
Are they father and son?

263
00:27:14,120 --> 00:27:14,960
Huh?

264
00:27:16,480 --> 00:27:18,840
<i>But he isn't in Wisut's family photo.</i>

265
00:27:19,760 --> 00:27:23,280
Exactly. What kind of son
plans a robbery at his own father's house?

266
00:27:23,360 --> 00:27:26,000
Hold on, everyone. Does that mean

267
00:27:26,080 --> 00:27:28,040
everything that happened

268
00:27:28,800 --> 00:27:30,840
was Mungkorn's plan?

269
00:27:31,560 --> 00:27:33,640
<i>Including Lin being sent</i>

270
00:27:34,680 --> 00:27:36,040
to help us

271
00:27:48,480 --> 00:27:50,840
and bringing us here to this base?

272
00:27:57,520 --> 00:28:01,600
<i>Welcome, everyone. From now on, call me</i>

273
00:28:02,400 --> 00:28:03,640
<i>Admin.</i>

274
00:28:06,360 --> 00:28:09,480
Right. We can't stay here anymore.

275
00:28:10,280 --> 00:28:14,200
He might be listening
or watching us right now.

276
00:28:34,680 --> 00:28:35,720
What is it, Koh?

277
00:28:41,280 --> 00:28:42,520
What's up, bro?

278
00:28:51,320 --> 00:28:52,600
Mungkorn?

279
00:29:00,880 --> 00:29:02,440
You're awake. How do you feel?

280
00:29:02,960 --> 00:29:04,480
Where are we?

281
00:29:05,480 --> 00:29:07,960
This is my old family house.

282
00:29:09,880 --> 00:29:11,680
What happened?

283
00:29:12,560 --> 00:29:14,680
The police raided the place.
You got knocked out.

284
00:29:25,440 --> 00:29:27,480
I happened to be there, so I got you out.

285
00:29:28,720 --> 00:29:31,080
Wait. How did you even find me?

286
00:29:31,920 --> 00:29:33,920
Lin contacted me.

287
00:29:34,520 --> 00:29:36,240
But that doesn't matter now.

288
00:29:36,320 --> 00:29:37,560
What about the others?

289
00:29:39,120 --> 00:29:41,960
I already contacted them. Everyone's safe.

290
00:29:49,960 --> 00:29:51,640
My phone? Where's my phone?

291
00:30:13,640 --> 00:30:15,000
{\an8}POWER OFF

292
00:30:18,560 --> 00:30:19,640
Your phone?

293
00:30:20,680 --> 00:30:23,200
You probably dropped it
during the mission.

294
00:30:25,480 --> 00:30:26,600
Just forget about it for now.

295
00:30:27,800 --> 00:30:29,360
Get some rest here until you've recovered.

296
00:30:29,440 --> 00:30:31,560
We'll meet up with the others later.

297
00:30:32,240 --> 00:30:33,400
Okay?

298
00:30:39,800 --> 00:30:42,480
I bought you some clothes.
Change if you need to.

299
00:30:45,560 --> 00:30:49,080
I'll go get you something to eat.

300
00:31:16,800 --> 00:31:20,320
How do you explain the source
of the 800 maillion baht in your safe?

301
00:31:20,400 --> 00:31:21,840
I'm a businessman.

302
00:31:22,360 --> 00:31:26,640
That money came from my business,
of course.

303
00:31:26,720 --> 00:31:30,760
That means you have documents
to verify all of it?

304
00:31:30,840 --> 00:31:33,200
All the documents are here.

305
00:31:33,920 --> 00:31:37,880
As we said, we will only submit them
to General Thammarong.

306
00:31:40,240 --> 00:31:42,080
Do you really think an ordinary person

307
00:31:42,160 --> 00:31:44,760
keeps that much cash stored at home?

308
00:31:44,840 --> 00:31:46,840
It's my money.

309
00:31:47,560 --> 00:31:50,000
Where I keep it is none of your business.

310
00:31:51,600 --> 00:31:53,680
You should worry
about your own situation instead.

311
00:31:54,280 --> 00:31:57,080
I heard you still have a large debt

312
00:31:57,160 --> 00:31:58,720
to pay off at home.

313
00:31:59,800 --> 00:32:02,120
If you need help, just say so.

314
00:32:03,720 --> 00:32:05,120
What did you just say?

315
00:32:06,040 --> 00:32:09,040
Nothing. I'm just trying to help.

316
00:32:09,960 --> 00:32:13,920
Now stop wasting my time.
Bring your superior to me.

317
00:32:21,280 --> 00:32:22,360
Captain, step outside.

318
00:32:23,280 --> 00:32:24,240
I'll handle this.

319
00:32:32,720 --> 00:32:35,720
Where are those documents?

320
00:32:38,880 --> 00:32:40,880
These documents prove
the source of all the funds,

321
00:32:41,480 --> 00:32:43,560
showing they came from
Mr. Wisut's export business

322
00:32:43,640 --> 00:32:46,080
and recycling operations.

323
00:32:53,120 --> 00:32:55,000
I'll give you time

324
00:32:55,680 --> 00:32:58,240
to review the evidence carefully.

325
00:32:59,800 --> 00:33:04,720
I hope this matter can be resolved soon.

326
00:33:10,640 --> 00:33:12,560
You're targeting the wrong person.

327
00:33:14,200 --> 00:33:17,400
Aren't you afraid of being charged
with bribing a law enforcement officer?

328
00:33:19,880 --> 00:33:21,400
It's no big deal.

329
00:33:21,480 --> 00:33:24,760
With your authority,
this case could easily be closed.

330
00:33:25,840 --> 00:33:28,360
Just tell me what you want.

331
00:33:28,440 --> 00:33:29,840
I can support you.

332
00:33:30,600 --> 00:33:34,520
Why don't we settle this,
so we're both happy?

333
00:33:37,000 --> 00:33:38,360
But I don't think

334
00:33:40,240 --> 00:33:42,400
this will end happily for you.

335
00:33:44,920 --> 00:33:46,880
You know, even if you refuse,

336
00:33:47,720 --> 00:33:50,200
someone else will accept my offer.

337
00:33:54,640 --> 00:33:56,640
I'd like to see

338
00:33:57,560 --> 00:33:59,480
who would dare accept it

339
00:34:00,920 --> 00:34:03,960
while I'm still on this case.

340
00:34:26,800 --> 00:34:27,760
Mr. Wisut.

341
00:34:28,640 --> 00:34:30,600
I'd like to withdraw from the case.

342
00:34:33,360 --> 00:34:34,360
What do you mean?

343
00:34:34,959 --> 00:34:37,920
I don't think Big Tum
is going to cooperate.

344
00:34:37,999 --> 00:34:39,400
And this case is too big.

345
00:34:39,999 --> 00:34:43,640
If they investigate everything,
we won't be able to protect ourselves.

346
00:34:46,600 --> 00:34:49,160
Useless trash. Get out of my sight.

347
00:34:49,240 --> 00:34:50,479
Leave!

348
00:34:53,200 --> 00:34:54,200
Sir.

349
00:34:54,280 --> 00:34:55,560
What now?

350
00:34:55,640 --> 00:34:58,080
This morning, Madam packed up
and left with Chin and Moei.

351
00:34:59,360 --> 00:35:01,240
-Where to?
-Europe, sir.

352
00:35:01,880 --> 00:35:05,840
She said she'll return
after you've dealt with this situation.

353
00:35:13,840 --> 00:35:15,720
Forget it. She's a gold digger.

354
00:35:16,320 --> 00:35:19,200
Get all the network leaders here
immediately.

355
00:35:19,800 --> 00:35:20,920
Yes, sir.

356
00:35:37,480 --> 00:35:38,960
Little Mungkorn's room.

357
00:36:16,320 --> 00:36:21,440
MY DREAM

358
00:36:23,200 --> 00:36:24,040
MY DREAM, MUNGKORN

359
00:36:28,920 --> 00:36:32,640
<i>THE GREED OF THE OLD FARMER</i>

360
00:36:39,520 --> 00:36:40,760
There you are.

361
00:36:41,920 --> 00:36:42,960
Feeling better?

362
00:36:45,800 --> 00:36:49,400
So this is Little Mungkorn's room?
Your drawings are interesting.

363
00:36:49,480 --> 00:36:52,200
What are you doing?
You can't touch things without asking.

364
00:36:54,480 --> 00:36:55,440
Fine.

365
00:36:56,280 --> 00:36:58,680
May I, Little Mungkorn?

366
00:36:59,960 --> 00:37:04,440
Enough. Come on. Let's eat.
I got us some food.

367
00:37:06,800 --> 00:37:09,320
Thanks, Little Mungkorn.

368
00:37:10,360 --> 00:37:11,400
Stop it.

369
00:37:26,600 --> 00:37:32,520
<i>THE GREED OF THE OLD FARMER</i>

370
00:37:44,840 --> 00:37:48,240
{\an8}I can't believe a guy
from a wealthy family like you

371
00:37:48,320 --> 00:37:50,200
{\an8}used to live in a place like this.

372
00:37:54,400 --> 00:37:56,920
I really love this house.

373
00:37:58,440 --> 00:38:00,360
I love it even more
than the one I live in now.

374
00:38:10,480 --> 00:38:11,680
Mungkorn.

375
00:38:12,400 --> 00:38:14,320
Can I ask you something?

376
00:38:17,200 --> 00:38:18,400
Was it because of me

377
00:38:19,200 --> 00:38:21,360
that you didn't go on the mission
last night?

378
00:38:25,400 --> 00:38:26,640
It wasn't because of that.

379
00:38:27,560 --> 00:38:28,880
Then why?

380
00:38:31,000 --> 00:38:33,600
I'll tell you when the time is right.

381
00:38:35,920 --> 00:38:37,040
Always with the secrets.

382
00:38:39,920 --> 00:38:41,560
I don't keep secrets from you, Risa.

383
00:38:42,240 --> 00:38:44,880
Some things just aren't meant
to be told yet.

384
00:38:49,840 --> 00:38:51,240
I'm sorry…

385
00:38:54,000 --> 00:38:56,120
for what I said that day.

386
00:39:02,400 --> 00:39:05,280
It's okay. I understand.

387
00:39:14,160 --> 00:39:15,080
Do you think

388
00:39:15,760 --> 00:39:17,560
Admin's plan will succeed?

389
00:39:20,920 --> 00:39:24,800
At Wisut's house,
we didn't even find the 800 million

390
00:39:24,880 --> 00:39:26,320
before the police showed up.

391
00:39:26,920 --> 00:39:30,400
If Wisut figures it out,
he won't let us off easily.

392
00:39:32,400 --> 00:39:34,920
Wisut won't make it out of this anyway.

393
00:39:35,720 --> 00:39:37,200
Why do you think that?

394
00:39:38,560 --> 00:39:42,120
Well, have you ever seen Admin fail?

395
00:39:59,200 --> 00:40:00,280
Chin.

396
00:40:02,840 --> 00:40:04,760
-Boss.
-Hey, you look tense.

397
00:40:04,840 --> 00:40:06,160
And you're not?

398
00:40:17,440 --> 00:40:18,520
Note.

399
00:40:19,480 --> 00:40:20,760
Hey, bro.

400
00:40:21,680 --> 00:40:23,720
-You good?
-Of course.

401
00:40:24,720 --> 00:40:27,440
-Yo!
-Yo!

402
00:40:28,240 --> 00:40:31,320
-Hey, what's up?
-Good, man.

403
00:40:31,400 --> 00:40:33,480
Damn it. We're screwed.

404
00:40:37,280 --> 00:40:38,600
Good evening, madam.

405
00:40:39,160 --> 00:40:40,960
What's up, madam.

406
00:40:41,040 --> 00:40:42,760
Hello, Boss Glod and Boss Chin.

407
00:40:42,840 --> 00:40:43,720
Good evening.

408
00:40:44,680 --> 00:40:46,160
Everyone's here.

409
00:40:46,240 --> 00:40:49,280
The rumors about the police raid
on Wisut's house must be true.

410
00:40:49,360 --> 00:40:52,440
We haven't seen all the big players
together in a long time.

411
00:40:53,160 --> 00:40:54,040
Yeah.

412
00:41:05,800 --> 00:41:07,680
I have a feeling today's going to bring
some aftershocks.

413
00:41:07,760 --> 00:41:10,280
What aftershocks?
The ground hasn't even shaken yet.

414
00:41:10,360 --> 00:41:13,080
Who says it hasn't? Just look at his face.

415
00:41:13,160 --> 00:41:14,680
You can tell

416
00:41:14,760 --> 00:41:16,160
something big already happened.

417
00:41:18,000 --> 00:41:20,800
You all already know
the police searched my house, right?

418
00:41:22,160 --> 00:41:23,920
That's why I called everyone here today.

419
00:41:24,520 --> 00:41:25,920
Why make such a big deal out of it?

420
00:41:26,000 --> 00:41:29,200
It's just one cop.
Whatever he wants, just pay him.

421
00:41:29,280 --> 00:41:31,040
How hard can that be?

422
00:41:31,640 --> 00:41:33,520
But Big Tum isn't like the others.

423
00:41:34,160 --> 00:41:35,720
No matter how much I offered,
he wouldn't take it.

424
00:41:35,800 --> 00:41:37,760
Whoa, boss.

425
00:41:38,280 --> 00:41:41,640
One cop isn't a big deal.
Just get rid of him. It's not that hard.

426
00:41:42,240 --> 00:41:43,040
Are you stupid?

427
00:41:44,040 --> 00:41:46,320
He's a high-ranking officer.

428
00:41:46,400 --> 00:41:49,200
And now, he's openly declared
himself my enemy.

429
00:41:49,280 --> 00:41:51,120
If anything happens to him,

430
00:41:51,200 --> 00:41:53,320
I'll be the first suspect.

431
00:41:53,400 --> 00:41:55,000
So what do you want us to do?

432
00:42:05,840 --> 00:42:07,320
We pause everything

433
00:42:08,520 --> 00:42:09,600
and let things cool down for now.

434
00:42:10,440 --> 00:42:11,480
Hold on, boss.

435
00:42:14,360 --> 00:42:15,320
Are you crazy?

436
00:42:15,920 --> 00:42:18,760
If we do that, do you know
how much money I'll lose?

437
00:42:19,680 --> 00:42:21,320
I won't accept that.

438
00:42:21,400 --> 00:42:23,840
Would you rather lose a little income now

439
00:42:23,920 --> 00:42:26,560
or lose everything later?

440
00:42:26,640 --> 00:42:27,720
-Huh?
-Wait, boss.

441
00:42:29,120 --> 00:42:30,080
You're misunderstanding something.

442
00:42:31,520 --> 00:42:32,800
Why should we take the risk?

443
00:42:32,880 --> 00:42:34,120
-Yeah.
-Right.

444
00:42:34,200 --> 00:42:38,040
Those cops crossed your line.
That's not our problem.

445
00:42:38,720 --> 00:42:42,000
And isn't it your job
to deal with the police for us?

446
00:42:42,080 --> 00:42:44,680
Don't forget, your cut

447
00:42:44,760 --> 00:42:46,200
isn't exactly small.

448
00:42:48,240 --> 00:42:52,400
Are you saying
you're turning your back on me?

449
00:43:06,440 --> 00:43:07,480
Yes.

450
00:43:08,040 --> 00:43:10,840
If things aren't getting any better,
what's the point of staying?

451
00:43:11,440 --> 00:43:12,280
Fine.

452
00:43:13,160 --> 00:43:15,320
If you don't appreciate
what I've done for you,

453
00:43:15,400 --> 00:43:18,000
then leave. Go wherever you want.

454
00:43:18,880 --> 00:43:21,880
But you know

455
00:43:22,880 --> 00:43:25,720
what happens between us after this, right?

456
00:43:28,840 --> 00:43:30,280
I do know.

457
00:43:30,360 --> 00:43:33,560
And I also know
you can't protect us anymore.

458
00:43:34,200 --> 00:43:36,200
Anyone who wants to stick
with a boss who has no future,

459
00:43:37,000 --> 00:43:40,320
who takes commissions
and calls them favors, go ahead.

460
00:43:40,400 --> 00:43:44,760
But I'm confident what I've paid you

461
00:43:44,840 --> 00:43:47,240
has long since exceeded
any so-called favors.

462
00:43:53,160 --> 00:43:54,400
Let's go.

463
00:43:59,280 --> 00:44:00,320
Sorry, boss.

464
00:44:01,000 --> 00:44:03,160
But I think Boss Glod is right.

465
00:44:08,240 --> 00:44:11,600
Fine. Go wherever you want!

466
00:44:11,680 --> 00:44:13,840
Don't ever show your faces to me again!

467
00:44:23,520 --> 00:44:27,120
Let's talk after you've cleaned up
this whole mess.

468
00:44:46,040 --> 00:44:47,000
So this is the house

469
00:44:47,960 --> 00:44:50,080
we're using as our new base?

470
00:44:50,760 --> 00:44:53,560
Yeah. We'll stay here for now.

471
00:44:54,600 --> 00:44:58,520
Not too bad. It's pretty nice and quiet.
Is this your house, Koh?

472
00:44:59,680 --> 00:45:01,640
Not my house. No idea whose it is.

473
00:45:01,720 --> 00:45:03,040
-Hey.
-Huh?

474
00:45:03,120 --> 00:45:04,880
This house was involved in a case
back when I was a cop.

475
00:45:04,960 --> 00:45:07,560
It's off the radar.
No one will find us here.

476
00:45:07,640 --> 00:45:09,360
By the way, can you hook up the power?

477
00:45:09,440 --> 00:45:13,200
Easy. I could do it with my eyes closed.

478
00:45:14,160 --> 00:45:15,040
Hey, Angpao.

479
00:45:15,120 --> 00:45:16,360
Do we have any tools in the car?

480
00:45:18,080 --> 00:45:19,720
-Hey.
-Yes?

481
00:45:19,800 --> 00:45:21,600
I asked if we have any tools in the car.

482
00:45:21,680 --> 00:45:24,200
Oh yeah. We do.

483
00:45:24,280 --> 00:45:26,720
-Bro, I'll help you. Alright?
-Huh?

484
00:45:26,800 --> 00:45:28,240
Angpao, you should get some rest.

485
00:45:28,760 --> 00:45:29,680
Okay?

486
00:45:30,440 --> 00:45:33,400
-Yeah.
-Are you sleepy?

487
00:45:36,200 --> 00:45:38,360
-Come on.
-How do we hook up the power?

488
00:45:38,440 --> 00:45:40,320
-Huh? With a match.
-How do we hook up the power?

489
00:45:40,400 --> 00:45:41,480
Oops!

490
00:45:58,360 --> 00:45:59,600
You're stressed about Mungkorn?

491
00:46:04,120 --> 00:46:06,840
Do you really think he betrayed us?

492
00:46:14,040 --> 00:46:14,920
I don't know.

493
00:46:15,880 --> 00:46:17,240
See?

494
00:46:18,080 --> 00:46:19,800
You're no different from everyone else.

495
00:46:22,240 --> 00:46:23,280
That's not what I mean.

496
00:46:25,160 --> 00:46:29,840
I mean, I don't know what he's thinking.

497
00:46:31,800 --> 00:46:33,760
The only way to know

498
00:46:33,840 --> 00:46:36,200
is to find those two.

499
00:46:36,800 --> 00:46:40,080
I already tried looking for Lin.
I couldn't find her.

500
00:46:41,280 --> 00:46:43,160
I don't know where else to look for clues.

501
00:46:48,760 --> 00:46:50,480
You're worried about Risa, aren't you?

502
00:46:51,880 --> 00:46:52,760
Yeah.

503
00:46:54,960 --> 00:46:56,000
You like her, don't you?

504
00:46:58,480 --> 00:47:00,160
There it is. I knew it.

505
00:47:03,440 --> 00:47:04,680
That's not it.

506
00:47:05,400 --> 00:47:08,160
I promised her I'd protect her.

507
00:47:09,000 --> 00:47:11,320
Wow, what a hero.

508
00:47:12,200 --> 00:47:13,560
When did you two have a moment?

509
00:47:16,440 --> 00:47:20,520
That's not it. It's just… You little punk.

510
00:47:20,600 --> 00:47:21,760
I came here to comfort you.

511
00:47:22,440 --> 00:47:24,680
Enough.

512
00:47:24,760 --> 00:47:25,920
Koh.

513
00:47:28,360 --> 00:47:29,640
You know

514
00:47:31,880 --> 00:47:33,400
Mungkorn likes Risa too, right?

515
00:47:39,480 --> 00:47:42,080
Koh! Koh! Angpao!

516
00:47:42,160 --> 00:47:43,840
Come look at this!

517
00:47:43,920 --> 00:47:45,480
-Hurry, Koh!
-<i>Last night,</i>

518
00:47:45,560 --> 00:47:48,320
<i>a group of intruders broke into the home</i>
<i>of Wisut Hema-a-thipat,</i>

519
00:47:48,400 --> 00:47:49,920
-<i>a businessman and owner of VS Group.</i>
-Look.

520
00:47:50,000 --> 00:47:54,400
<i>After receiving the report,</i>
<i>police arrived at the scene,</i>

521
00:47:54,480 --> 00:47:57,080
<i>but the suspects managed to escape.</i>

522
00:47:58,240 --> 00:48:01,680
<i>But the incident didn't end there.</i>
<i>After police searched the scene</i>

523
00:48:01,760 --> 00:48:05,520
<i>and collected evidence, they discovered</i>

524
00:48:05,600 --> 00:48:07,520
<i>over 800 million baht</i>

525
00:48:07,600 --> 00:48:09,960
<i>hidden inside a secret safe in the house.</i>

526
00:48:11,640 --> 00:48:14,960
There really was that much money in there?

527
00:48:15,560 --> 00:48:19,040
-What would you like?
-One pack of water, please.

528
00:48:19,120 --> 00:48:20,120
Sure.

529
00:48:20,200 --> 00:48:25,120
<i>This case is under the responsibility</i>
<i>of Pol.Lt.Gen. Thammarong Intharasa,</i>

530
00:48:25,200 --> 00:48:27,000
<i>better known as Big Tum.</i>

531
00:48:27,080 --> 00:48:30,920
<i>He's the officer nicknamed</i>
<i>"The Mad Dog Who Never Lets Go,"</i>

532
00:48:31,000 --> 00:48:33,520
<i>and he's closed many major cases before.</i>

533
00:48:34,200 --> 00:48:37,600
{\an8}<i>The suspect denies that the source</i>
<i>of the more than 800 million baht</i>

534
00:48:38,200 --> 00:48:40,920
<i>came from the online gambling sites</i>
<i>currently under investigation.</i>

535
00:48:41,720 --> 00:48:43,920
<i>He claims it came from</i>
<i>their legitimate businesses.</i>

536
00:48:45,000 --> 00:48:47,520
Maybe Mungkorn really
is working with the police.

537
00:48:50,040 --> 00:48:52,480
He planned to have the cops
take down both Wisut

538
00:48:53,080 --> 00:48:55,880
and all of us at the same time.
It was his plan.

539
00:48:58,120 --> 00:48:59,240
That bastard.

540
00:48:59,320 --> 00:49:02,800
<i>The suspect is gathering documents</i>
<i>to explain the source of the funds</i>

541
00:49:03,520 --> 00:49:09,440
<i>and intends to fight the case. We're</i>
<i>confident in the evidence we've gathered.</i>

542
00:49:09,520 --> 00:49:12,000
-Excuse me, sir.
-<i>We are preparing the case file to submit</i>

543
00:49:12,080 --> 00:49:14,480
-<i>to the prosecutor for further action.</i>
-Would you like anything else?

544
00:49:16,080 --> 00:49:17,320
Huh?

545
00:49:21,400 --> 00:49:23,720
<i>This case is under the responsibility--</i>

546
00:49:23,800 --> 00:49:25,920
Mungkorn, have you seen the news?

547
00:49:26,000 --> 00:49:27,680
The police found the money at that house.

548
00:49:27,760 --> 00:49:29,000
I saw it.

549
00:49:29,080 --> 00:49:30,880
Admin really never fails,
just like you said.

550
00:49:30,960 --> 00:49:33,600
Then we don't have
to keep hiding anymore, right?

551
00:49:34,200 --> 00:49:35,960
Let's go back and meet up with everyone.

552
00:49:37,280 --> 00:49:41,200
I talked to Angpao.
They said we should stay hidden for now.

553
00:49:41,280 --> 00:49:43,720
Once everything is sorted out,
we'll regroup.

554
00:49:44,400 --> 00:49:45,960
Oh, really?

555
00:49:47,040 --> 00:49:49,920
I'll go get bowls for the noodles.

556
00:49:54,480 --> 00:49:55,880
ANGPAO

557
00:49:55,960 --> 00:49:57,280
Angpao's calling.

558
00:50:03,360 --> 00:50:04,240
Don't.

559
00:50:08,200 --> 00:50:09,120
Why?

560
00:50:26,680 --> 00:50:29,040
Hello, Mung. Where the hell are you?

561
00:50:29,120 --> 00:50:30,320
Why weren't you answering?

562
00:50:32,320 --> 00:50:34,200
Angpao, it's me.

563
00:50:35,080 --> 00:50:36,680
Ris? Ris!

564
00:50:37,520 --> 00:50:40,320
I'm okay. Is everyone safe?

565
00:50:40,400 --> 00:50:42,680
Yeah. Hey, Ris.

566
00:50:42,760 --> 00:50:44,240
<i>Where are you right now?</i>

567
00:50:44,760 --> 00:50:45,920
I'm with Mungkorn right now.

568
00:50:49,320 --> 00:50:52,560
Ris, don't trust him yet.

569
00:50:54,560 --> 00:50:55,400
What do you mean?

570
00:50:55,480 --> 00:50:58,720
Just tell me where you are.
We'll come get you right away.

571
00:50:59,720 --> 00:51:00,800
What are you talking about?

572
00:51:01,400 --> 00:51:03,000
That night at Wisut's house,

573
00:51:03,680 --> 00:51:06,800
Koh said he saw Mungkorn take you away.

574
00:51:08,320 --> 00:51:12,800
Now we know who Admin really is.
It's Mungkorn.

575
00:51:18,560 --> 00:51:19,640
Angpao.

576
00:51:22,360 --> 00:51:24,480
I'll find a way to contact you again.

577
00:51:25,200 --> 00:51:28,600
Get ready to come pick me up.
That's all for now.

578
00:51:29,200 --> 00:51:30,600
I need to talk to Mungkorn.

579
00:51:33,640 --> 00:51:35,080
Wait, Ris. Ris!

580
00:51:40,160 --> 00:51:41,440
Why did you lie to me?

581
00:51:46,520 --> 00:51:48,440
Are you finally going
to tell me everything?

582
00:51:53,360 --> 00:51:54,560
Well, Ris…

583
00:51:55,800 --> 00:51:57,840
I was planning to tell you
the whole truth anyway.

584
00:51:57,920 --> 00:51:59,480
Then tell me!

585
00:52:02,280 --> 00:52:03,520
Angpao said you're Admin.

586
00:52:12,480 --> 00:52:14,920
Yes. I'm Admin.

587
00:52:16,920 --> 00:52:18,600
Why would you do that?

588
00:52:24,360 --> 00:52:28,240
If you don't answer me now, we're done.

589
00:52:30,800 --> 00:52:32,560
The reason I created Admin was because…

590
00:52:35,400 --> 00:52:36,920
I wanted to stop my father.

591
00:52:38,080 --> 00:52:39,280
What do you mean?

592
00:52:40,320 --> 00:52:41,320
Wisut.

593
00:52:42,480 --> 00:52:43,320
Wisut is my father.

594
00:52:45,920 --> 00:52:46,920
Then,

595
00:52:47,000 --> 00:52:49,680
why didn't you ever tell us?

596
00:52:49,760 --> 00:52:53,280
Because what I'm doing
means destroying my own father.

597
00:52:53,360 --> 00:52:55,840
Besides, once everything was over,
once the plan succeeded,

598
00:52:55,920 --> 00:52:58,360
everyone would've gotten their share,
and Admin would've disappeared.

599
00:52:58,440 --> 00:52:59,600
There was no reason for anyone

600
00:52:59,680 --> 00:53:02,480
to know who Admin really was.

601
00:53:03,080 --> 00:53:04,240
And yes.

602
00:53:04,760 --> 00:53:07,120
I was the one who contacted the police.

603
00:53:08,520 --> 00:53:09,480
What?

604
00:53:09,560 --> 00:53:11,840
But I never meant
for it to turn out like this, Ris.

605
00:53:11,920 --> 00:53:14,800
I didn't know the police
would move in early. I didn't know

606
00:53:14,880 --> 00:53:17,600
the whole plan would fall apart.

607
00:53:18,880 --> 00:53:20,560
I…

608
00:53:22,760 --> 00:53:24,440
I never planned for any of this.

609
00:53:26,840 --> 00:53:27,680
Mungkorn.

610
00:53:29,200 --> 00:53:30,960
You know what?

611
00:53:32,360 --> 00:53:33,920
In my life,

612
00:53:34,520 --> 00:53:38,480
besides my dad, I had no one.

613
00:53:40,080 --> 00:53:43,760
When my dad disappeared, I was all alone.

614
00:53:43,840 --> 00:53:45,640
Until I met you guys.

615
00:53:47,480 --> 00:53:50,680
You and Angpao
were the two people I trusted most.

616
00:53:52,200 --> 00:53:55,400
And you still did this to me.
How am I supposed to trust you now?

617
00:53:56,560 --> 00:53:59,040
-Ris…
-Enough. Don't say another word.

618
00:53:59,960 --> 00:54:02,240
-I'm sorry.
-Don't come near me.

619
00:54:03,120 --> 00:54:06,040
Don't apologize. Don't say anything else.

620
00:54:08,920 --> 00:54:11,720
I don't care what happened
between you and your father.

621
00:54:11,800 --> 00:54:14,280
But you should never have dragged
other people into it.

622
00:54:14,360 --> 00:54:17,720
How many times have you
almost gotten everyone killed?

623
00:54:17,800 --> 00:54:20,680
You're so damn selfish, Mungkorn!

624
00:54:25,280 --> 00:54:26,520
Don't follow me!

625
00:55:04,000 --> 00:55:06,600
Sir.

626
00:55:08,440 --> 00:55:09,600
We've arrived.

627
00:55:13,400 --> 00:55:16,120
LITTLE MUNGKORN'S ROOM

628
00:55:19,120 --> 00:55:22,600
<i>How many times have you</i>
<i>almost gotten everyone killed?</i>

629
00:55:22,680 --> 00:55:25,120
<i>You're so damn selfish, Mungkorn!</i>

630
00:55:31,960 --> 00:55:34,280
<i>I don't care what happened</i>
<i>between you and your father.</i>

631
00:55:34,360 --> 00:55:35,280
<i>THE GREED OF THE OLD FARMER</i>

632
00:55:35,360 --> 00:55:37,640
<i>But you should never have dragged</i>
<i>other people into it.</i>

633
00:55:46,840 --> 00:55:50,200
{\an8}My world is white. But yours is black.

634
00:55:50,280 --> 00:55:52,080
{\an8}It's the same world.

635
00:55:52,160 --> 00:55:54,160
{\an8}You just carry the same scent I do,

636
00:55:54,240 --> 00:55:55,440
{\an8}the scent of greed.

637
00:55:55,520 --> 00:55:58,480
{\an8}This is the flash drive
Wisut gave to his son.

638
00:55:58,560 --> 00:56:00,520
{\an8}It contains evidence

639
00:56:00,600 --> 00:56:04,800
{\an8}that can bring down
the entire nationwide gambling network.

640
00:56:04,880 --> 00:56:07,280
{\an8}Do you even care about this country?

641
00:56:07,360 --> 00:56:09,160
{\an8}<i>But if you accept my offer,</i>

642
00:56:09,240 --> 00:56:12,840
{\an8}<i>I'll retrieve it for you</i>
<i>without you having to lift a finger.</i>

643
00:56:13,960 --> 00:56:15,800
{\an8}Glad to see you again.

644
00:56:15,880 --> 00:56:18,120
{\an8}Risa and Angpao
have been captured by Louis.

645
00:56:18,200 --> 00:56:19,400
{\an8}I need help.

646
00:56:19,480 --> 00:56:20,360
{\an8}What are you doing?

647
00:56:20,440 --> 00:56:21,960
{\an8}Blame your friend

648
00:56:22,040 --> 00:56:24,240
{\an8}for thinking someone like me
wouldn't go all the way.

649
00:56:24,320 --> 00:56:25,640
{\an8}See you in the next life.

650
00:57:17,000 --> 00:57:19,720
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn

